  unit: { count: 202, covers: "Counts are what this WU added or rewrote, not the suites they live in (1065 Vitest tests in 55 files and 42 shell tests are green at the tip, with the core's 246 untouched). The two entries the reading round proposed and this WU built: ChoiceTiles +13 — every option rendered, exactly one taken, the group as one tab stop, arrows moving focus without committing and stopping at the ends, the value prop as the only source of what is taken, the disabled group, and a row that wraps rather than scrolling. TaskStep +7 — the number and title, a purpose line where one is given and none where it is not, a state rendered only where a resolver produced one, the dimmed variant keeping its number, and the slot below the state. Both carried through the collection's four oracles: the barrel exports exactly the TSDoc's roster, every name mounts standalone, every @avoid redirect resolves, and no docstring names anything the tree cannot reach. The shell +9 — the combined act as one elevation on macOS with the proxy write following the trust write, one UAC prompt on Windows, a host with no automatic path, the two single commands proved unchanged by the combined one, the three wordings macOS and Windows use for a dismissed or unshowable prompt, a real failure that is not one of them, the empty-stderr fallback, the reading that carries the address it classified and the one that has none — plus the replacement ask, which names the proxy and says it does not come back. The copy, as literal assertions against the archived run's copy table: Onboarding.test.tsx rewritten to 58 tests over the title and purpose, the question, the six task states of this machine, the un-probeable promise, the primary action and its one-prompt line, the cancelled prompt and its disclosure, the foreign-proxy sentence with and without an address, the network task's single consequence line, the refusal, the arriving remedy and the end — with the seven machine words asserted ABSENT over all eight platforms rather than spot-checked, each task's state traced to the probe, the traffic layer or the reach state it names, the dimming rule off-machine, the Simulator's two stores, the manual route as the one alternative to the one button, the address offer, the probe row's scope, the tick's scope and the single scroller. setup.test.ts +38 over the platform vocabulary — the device each platform is called, the host naming itself, where a website is opened on each, the promise wording, the network task's title, and the machine words absent from every platform's own strings. verdicts.test.ts rewritten — all seventeen states the three resolvers return, asserted literally, each against StatusLine's ~40-char contract." }
  integration: { count: 70, covers: "The seams this WU moves, asserted where the screen sits inside App against the API stub and a mocked invoke — no half observable from a unit test of either side. F27: Set up this Mac fetches the PEM and invokes the one combined command with the split address, and no set_proxy runs beside it; the Simulator's proxy-only action still invokes set_proxy on its own, and its reversal still invokes unset_proxy. F18: a refusal crosses the IPC boundary as a refusal — a rejection is an arbitrary value, so the test asserts the structured failure survives it, the screen words the one the user caused, the tool's text stays under a disclosure, and a real failure keeps the OS's own words and the manual route. F17 in all three of its cases: a foreign proxy is confirmed before it is replaced and a refusal writes nothing, an allowed replacement goes through once, and a machine with no proxy is asked nothing. F22: the list's first paint after the machine's captured event says setup worked, it dismisses, set up another device returns to setup and takes the banner with it, and a launch that finds capture already working announces nothing. Plus the seams the rebuilt screen inherits, re-pointed at what it renders: the save writes the certificate under the name the steps run against, the probes drive both tasks and are re-read by check again and by window focus, a tunnel settles the last task and puts its remedy beside it, and the reach seam's confirm, refusal, arming, disarming and naming are unchanged." }
  e2e: { waived: "The epic owes the e2e and W6 writes it, against the screen this WU leaves — the spine rewritten on the platform axis with a coverage map over the 8 assertions the current spec holds. ui/e2e/specs/onboarding.spec.ts is stale at this tip on purpose: its assertions describe the screen W3 built, and re-pointing them here would land a spec asserting a shape one WU of the epic still has to close around. Recorded as the epic's, per the charter's additive rule." }
